# Rank 1252 / CVE-2026-42557 (GHSA-mqcg-5x36-vfcg): JupyterLab's HTML
# sanitizer allowlisted `data-commandlinker-command` / `data-commandlinker-args`
# on `<button>` elements, and CommandLinker registered a single delegated
# click listener on document.body that walked up from event.target, read
# those two attributes off whatever element was clicked, and executed the
# named command with no check that the element came from trusted JupyterLab
# UI rather than sanitized (but attacker-authored) notebook output. A saved
# notebook with an HTML cell output containing such a button triggered an
# arbitrary JupyterLab command -- including kernel code execution -- on a
# single click (CWE-79). Fix commit 5d9cb8c634e0 (the advisory's own
# c5f522db11d0 is the identical fix rebased onto the 4.5.x release branch)
# makes `_evtClick` async and gates execution behind `_isTrusted(target)` --
# an in-memory WeakMap populated only via the new `markTrusted()` API --
# plus a confirmation dialog (`_requestTrust`/
# `showCommandLinkerTrustDialog`), and adds a sanitizer toggle
# `setAllowCommandLinker(false)`; the data flow itself (attribute read ->
# `.execute(command, args)`) survives the fix by design, because trusted
# buttons still dispatch through the same call.
#
# ATTENTION, no discrimination. The attribute read is labelled now:
# domInput2650 (bindings/javascript/mfb63017a.vyql) emits code.DomInput at
# every `getAttribute()` result, and `.execute` matches sqlExecution131 as
# code.SqlExecution off the method name alone, so VYQL-INJ-001 fires high on
# the vulnerable flow -- in this spec pair and in the real checkout
# (packages/apputils, 3x --cache off runs per revision, timeout 180,
# --max-ram 6GB, no ceiling abort): the vulnerable revision reports
# VYQL-INJ-001 at src/commandlinker.ts:176 -> :185 (4 findings total: also
# 2 VYQL-CRY-003 in windowresolver.ts, 1 VYQL-INJ-009 in toolbar/factory.ts)
# and the fixed revision reports VYQL-INJ-001 twice -- the same flow plus
# one through the fix's own `_findTrustCommand` return into
# `.execute(trustCommand)` (5 findings total). The patched revision scores
# higher than the vulnerable one, so promotion is measured out: no rule
# separates the pair, and the -flags only view reports zero review-concept
# flags on either revision. The only separating signal available is the
# fix's own trust API (`markTrusted`/`_isTrusted`/`_requestTrust`) -- the
# fixing commit's own layout as a discriminator -- while generalising the
# source to any DOM-attribute read inside a delegated handler would flag
# ordinary, safe event delegation (Bootstrap `data-toggle`, htmx `hx-*`)
# broadly. code.HtmlSanitizerLogicReview and code.UnsafeEmbeddableAllowlist
# stay silent because the sanitizer does exactly what its allowlist says;
# the danger is unrelated application code trusting one permitted attribute
# as a command.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-no-discrimination; both tests pin the
# identical VYQL-INJ-001 firing (the trust gate is invisible to the taint
# path) plus the silence of the nearest-theme rules

test "rank1252: _evtClick dispatches a data-commandlinker-command attribute with no trust check"
  lang javascript
  file commandlinker.ts
  expect VYQL-INJ-001
  reject VYQL-INJ-009
  reject_review code.HtmlSanitizerLogicReview
  code
  ```
  class CommandLinker {
    private _evtClick(event: MouseEvent): void {
      let target = event.target as HTMLElement;
      while (target && target.parentElement) {
        if (target.hasAttribute('data-commandlinker-command')) {
          event.preventDefault();
          const command = target.getAttribute('data-commandlinker-command');
          if (!command) {
            return;
          }
          const argsValue = target.getAttribute('data-commandlinker-args');
          let args = {};
          if (argsValue) {
            args = JSON.parse(argsValue);
          }
          void this._commands.execute(command, args);
          return;
        }
        target = target.parentElement;
      }
    }

    private _commands: any;
  }
  ```

test "rank1252: _evtClick asks for trust before dispatching an unmarked node"
  lang javascript
  file commandlinker.ts
  expect VYQL-INJ-001
  reject VYQL-INJ-009
  reject_review code.HtmlSanitizerLogicReview
  code
  ```
  class CommandLinker {
    private async _evtClick(event: MouseEvent): Promise<void> {
      let target = event.target as HTMLElement;
      while (target && target.parentElement) {
        if (target.hasAttribute('data-commandlinker-command')) {
          event.preventDefault();
          const command = target.getAttribute('data-commandlinker-command');
          if (!command) {
            return;
          }
          const argsValue = target.getAttribute('data-commandlinker-args');
          let args = {};
          if (argsValue) {
            args = JSON.parse(argsValue);
          }

          if (!this._isTrusted(target)) {
            const trustAction = await this._requestTrust(command, args);
            if (trustAction === 'cancel') {
              return;
            }
          }

          void this._commands.execute(command, args);
          return;
        }
        target = target.parentElement;
      }
    }

    private _isTrusted(target: HTMLElement): boolean {
      let node: HTMLElement | null = target;
      while (node) {
        if (this._trustedBoundaries.has(node)) {
          return true;
        }
        node = node.parentElement;
      }
      return false;
    }

    private async _requestTrust(command: string, args: any): Promise<string> {
      return 'cancel';
    }

    private _commands: any;
    private _trustedBoundaries = new WeakMap<HTMLElement, true>();
  }
  ```
